"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Collecting_grapes?oldid=36440375",
"Collecting grapes",
"collecting-harmonic-dust.standard",
"Harmonic dust can be obtained by playing harps within the Ithell district of Prifddinas. Harps are a very low effort way of training crafting, and the harmonic dust has many uses. Once you have acquired all of the crystal items you need, the dust can be made into items and sold for profit - this is a nice supplementary income whilst training crafting. If you're planning on staying at harps for many hours, it's worth buying crystal armour seeds or crystal weapon seeds earlier than you need as they can take awhile to buy on the GE. Approximately 750 dust can be obtained an hour without VoS (or artificer's measure) at level 99 Crafting.",
"Ithell district of Prifddinas",
"75 Crafting",
"Artificer's measure (recommended)",
"Money making guide/Collecting harmonic dust",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Collecting_harmonic_dust?oldid=36917141",
"Collecting harmonic dust",
"collecting-honeycomb.standard",
"Honeycombs are used to make honey badger pouches. They can be extracted from the beehives East of Manor Farm behind the large pen. This requires insect repellent, which can be stored in the toolbelt. Extracting honeycomb is a click-intensive process as you have to right-click and select \"Honey\" for each one you want, though you can skip the animation of the character collecting the honeycomb by re-clicking the honey option on the same beehive.",
"Fill your inventory and run to the Manor Farm bank chest and back, and repeat. Use of Surge will decrease the time needed to bank. If the player has access to a Beast of Burden this can be used to further increase the amount of honeycombs that can be gathered per trip.",
"The Ardougne lodestone is located directly south-west of Manor Farm.",
"If the medium Ardougne achievements have been completed, the Manor farm Teleport or the Ardougne cloak 2/3 can be used to teleport to Manor Farm once per day.",
"If the elite Ardougne achievements have been completed, the Manor farm Teleport or the Ardougne cloak 4 can be used to teleport to Manor Farm without any daily limit.",
"Skills necklace can be used to travel directly there.",
"Manor Farm",
"Insect repellent",
"Money making guide/Collecting honeycomb",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Collecting_honeycomb?oldid=36473406",
"Collecting honeycomb",
"collecting-jangerberries.standard",
"Four jangerberries, used to make zamorak brews, can be found on an ogre-infested island north of Gu'Tanoth.",
"Starting at the Castle Wars lobby with only a rope in your inventory and a ring of duelling equipped, run straight east to the island. Use Surge to either cross the bridge or after the point where the character last turns before the lake to speed up the trip. Then, use the rope on the tree branch, jumping over to the island (this will use up the rope).",
"The ogres on the island are not aggressive. Run in a circle, continually collecting the berries. When your inventory is full, teleport back to the lobby with your duelling ring, bank, and repeat. A bank preset can be used to speed banking up.",
"Use Home Teleport to Yanille lodestone.",
"Use Watchtower Teleport, toggled to Yanille after completing the Ardougne Set Tasks - Hard.",
"Use Ring of duelling teleport to Castle Wars.",
"To the north lies the Fight Arena, the Tree Gnome Village, a Monastery, Port Khazard and (further north) East Ardougne.",
"Yanille",
"The Yanille lodestone is the closest to the fairy ring network.",
"The Edgeville lodestone, however, is the closest to both a bank and a fairy ring.",
"The Al Kharid lodestone is closest to the gnome glider network.",
"The Port Sarim lodestone is closest to a charter ship port.",
"Lodestone Network",
"Ogre island south-west of Yanille / lodestone",
"10 Agility",
"Member",
"Money making guide/Collecting jangerberries",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Collecting_jangerberries?oldid=36473386",
"Collecting jangerberries",
"collecting-limpwurt-roots.standard",
"There are 4 spawns of limpwurt root in the resource dungeon located within Edgeville Dungeon where the Hill Giants are. To access the dungeon efficiently, a brass key is needed to enter the hut just west of Cooks' Guild. Then, head south to the room containing Hill Giants and limpwurt root spawns.",
"As they are level 26, Hill Giants are aggressive to any player with a combat level of 52 or less, which may be an annoyance to the gathering process. It is therefore recommended to have at least level 53 combat.",
"On an averagely populated world, each limpwurt root re-spawns at a rate of around 56 seconds. However, as it takes less than 15 seconds to collect all 4 roots, it is recommended to constantly switch between worlds, effectively eliminating the respawn time. Once the inventory is full, head back up the shortcut to Varrock and bank the limpwurt roots at the Grand Exchange. Use of Surge will allow the player to make faster trips.",
"Edgeville Dungeon hill giant resource dungeon",
"20 Dungeoneering",
"53 Combat (recommended)",
"Money making guide/Collecting limpwurt roots",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Collecting_limpwurt_roots?oldid=36473274",
"Collecting limpwurt roots",
"collecting-memory-shards.standard",
"Memory shards may be obtained from pickpocketing, checking hunter traps, or planting seeds, when the relevant passive perk (for each method) is active from the Memorial to Guthix. When memory shards are earned, it will prompt the message \"You find a small fragment of a memory\".",
"Memory shards can also be obtained in the Hall of Memories while harvesting memories when the buff from getting close to a recollection butterfly is active.",
"Each time you obtain memory shards the amount varies, so it's possible to get as low as 400 and as high as 800 per hour depending on luck. For this guide 600 memory shards has been used as an average obtained per hour.",
"Memory shards can be converted into porters, with the best conversation rate being Sign of the porter IV with 1.25 charges per shard.",
"Profit per hour column is based on converting 600 memory shards.",
"No fixed destination is specified for this method. Choose a convenient place for the activity.",
"Anywhere",
"Money making guide/Collecting memory shards",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Collecting_memory_shards?oldid=36814030",
"Collecting memory shards",
"collecting-mort-myre-fungi.standard",
"Collecting mort myre fungi is very profitable as it is the secondary ingredient for making super energy potions. While wearing Morytania legs, players will receive double the amount of fungi when collecting. However, make sure there are at least two inventory spaces when collecting, otherwise players will only receive one fungus. Casting bloom affects rotting objects in the 8 squares around the player and consumes between 10 and 60 prayer points (though if the player only has 1 prayer point left, bloom can still be cast). Players should use a location surrounded by 3 rotting logs to increase the chances of obtaining mort myre fungus. An Ivandis flail or blessed silver sickle can be placed on the action bar to cast bloom with hotkeys. Players should use the three logs south of the Deposit Box as those are the most efficient. Gathering the fungus by prioritising the logs in the order of South-west, west, then East, you can cast bloom as soon as the mushrooms on the east log disappears, even though your character doesn't appear to be in the center yet. If the fungus on the logs disappears, it indicates that your character has reached that point even if it isn't shown. Using this, you will increase your fungus output by a decent amount.",
"Fairy ring BKR is located within the swamp.",
"Fairy ring ALQ is located in the Haunted Woods. Run southwest to enter the swamp area.",
"Fairy ring CKS is located just north of Mort Myre. Run south through the gate to enter the swamp.",
"Upon reaching a combined total level of 100 in Temple Trekking, the gate at the north end of Mort Myre may also be used to quick-travel to the Nature Grotto near the south end of the swamp.",
"For people that haven't completed Deadliest Catch: first, use the fairy ring network to teleport to BKR. Run west until you see three rotting logs, as shown in the image above. Drink a dose of prayer renewal, stand in the middle of the 3 rotting logs and cast bloom. Mort myre fungi will not spawn every time. Always pick the northern log last because when picked, you will return to the middle, removing the need to click back. After a full inventory, teleport to the TzHaar Fight Cave with the TokKul-Zo to bank and repeat using the fairy ring just north. Alternatively, if you haven't got a TokKul-Zo, use the fairy ring to bank in Zanaris, although this is slightly slower.",
"Alternatively, players who complete the easy Ardougne achievements (Requires: Biohazard, Gertrude's Cat, Monk's Friend, Plague City, Tower of Life; 15 Fishing, 16 Thieving, 10 Construction), can use the Kandarin monastery Teleport after collecting fungi (but before banking with the TokKul-Zo ) to recharge their prayer point for free. The Kandarin monastery Teleport is a one click teleport spell that isn't interrupted by attacking ghasts unlike the TokKul-Zo. Return with a fairy ring as mentioned above.",
"Mort Myre Swamp",
"40 Thieving",
"36 Woodcutting",
"Silver sickle (b) or equivalent",
"NATURE_SPIRIT",
