"crafting-clockwork.using-taverley-lodestone",
"This article assumes the Lodestone Network is used to teleport to the Taverley lodestone and enter the player-owned house there (House Teleport can be used with 40 Magic, it is faster but consume runes), and a Beast of Burden is not used. Banking can be done via various teleportation methods (e.g. ring of duelling, or a mounted amulet of glory in the Quest Hall requiring 47 Construction). Each trip can be done within 2 minutes (30 trips an hour assumed).",
"Alternatively, if you have access to the Ithell district and an attuned crystal teleport seed, you can teleport to the Ithell district bank chest directly and then move east to the nearby POH portal.",
"Using Taverley lodestone",
"crafting-cosmic-runes.standard",
"Using the TokKul-Zo and fairy rings, you can make about 50 trips to the cosmic altar per hour. With 59 Runecrafting (giving double cosmic runes) and especially 75 Runecrafting (giving access to the giant pouch), this can be highly profitable.",
"Start out at the TzHaar Fight Cave bank in TzHaar City. Unload pure essence and store it in your pouches, then take out essence for your inventory. Run north and use the fairy ring to teleport to Zanaris. From there, run south to the agility shortcut -- if you have 66 Agility, go through both of them, although you may get stuck and take a small amount of damage before passing through. Run further south and enter the mysterious ruins, and then go directly to the altar. Craft your essence in your inventory and pouches, and then teleport back to the Fight Cave with your TokKul-Zo. If you are unwilling or unable to complete The Elder Kiln to gain the TokKul-Zo, it is possible to use the Wilderness Sword, starting at the Edgeville Bank and running across the river to the fairy ring there. This method is likely to be a little less efficient.",
"With this method you can craft about 2700 essence per hour, but without the giant pouch that will drop to about 2150.",
"Break a cosmic altar teleport tablet. It teleports the player to the ruins.",
"Use any fairy ring or a portable fairy ring to teleport to Zanaris and go south to the ruins. There are jutting walls that can be traversed with level 46 or 66 Agility to get to the ruins faster.",
"Cosmic altar",
"The quest Lost City is required for any and all methods of accessing Zanaris.",
"Skill portal tuned to the Zanaris fairy ring (requires completion of A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift).",
"Grace of the elves teleport, with a tuned Max Guild portal (requires completion of A Fairy Tale III - Battle at Ork's Rift).",
"Enter the hut in Lumbridge Swamp while holding a Dramen staff or lunar staff.",
