"crafting-soul-runes.with-catalytic-anima-stones",
"Assumes the guide's 5.4 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"The numbers listed assumes using expansive pouch, the Infinity ethereal outfit, the Abyssal Titan, and running 5.4 trips per hour while using the Powerburst of sorcery and catalytic anima stones every time you go through the abyss. It also assumes that the player has Wilderness elite tasks complete for Magical thread as well as using urns with the urn enhancer.",
"Profit can be greater or lesser depending on various factors such as how much attention is paid, the player's runecrafting level, boosts used or not used, quests completed, and speed while banking.",
"With optimised dives and surges, one can expect around 5.62–5.79 fully charged soul altars an hour, while without using any mobility abilities, one can expect 5.41–5.57 trips an hour.",
"Using the expansive pouch, an abyssal titan, and the full infinity ethereal outfit, a total of 126 pure essence can be brought, meaning three additional items can be taken each trip and still fill and charge 100 pure essence each time. For example, If a Brooch of the Gods is not owned, the player may bring a stack of Decorated runecrafting urns (empty), and a powerburst of sorcery or crystal binding rod with a portable fairy ring equipped. Any partially filled urns of the same type in the players inventory will be pulled from the bank and into the players inventory when they gain the relevant experience.",
"Fairy ring CKQ teleports into the west side of the Menaphos Imperial district, near the fountain entrance.",
"Use Menaphos lodestone teleport and run west (along the southside of the pyramid).",
"Leela's favour to imperial district and run west (along the southside of the pyramid).",
"Players with tier 6 reputation in the Imperial district can access the bank chest near the entrance of the Grand Library. The Imperial district teleport tablet places the player close to the chest, allowing players to use the two in conjunction to charge the altar without the use of the Abyss or fairy rings.",
"Make sure PvP is toggled off by talking to Vala in Edgeville before entering low-level Wilderness. The Mage of Zamorak is located near the source of the River Lum.",
