"farming-marigolds.standard",
"Can be done every 20 minutes; a run takes about 3 minutes.",
"20 minutes",
"As a tertiary ingredient used in the Summoning skill, marigolds are always in demand. And with Farming being almost the only source of marigolds, the demand is not always met. Farming marigolds can thus be somewhat profitable for low-level players, as it requires only level 2 Farming and is even available to non-members.",
"Members have access to four farming patches in which marigolds can be farmed - one near Falador, one near Port Phasmatys, one in Catherby and one at the Manor Farm. Only the one near Falador is available to free players, so if you're not a member you'll make roughly one quarter of the profits listed here. Apart from membership, none of these patches have any requirements to access, but the one by Port Phasmatys can be time-consuming to get to without the ectophial or a modified farmer's hat (the latter of which can only be used three times a day) - the easiest way to get there without either of those is teleporting to the Canifis lodestone, though skipping the patch might be a better option. The Falador patch also takes a little bit of time to reach without the Explorer's ring 3 or the South Falador Teleport spell, although the Draynor Village lodestone is reasonably close by. The Manor Farm and Catherby patches are easy to reach with the lodestone Network, and should always be used.",
"When you expect the marigolds to be fully grown (roughly 20 minutes after planting), head to each of the patches you used and pick the marigolds. If they died, clear the patch instead. If they are alive but diseased, the nearby farmers sell plant cure for 25 coins if you talk to them - you won't get any marigolds this time around, but it saves you a seed. Once you have picked the flowers or cleared the patch, plant another marigold seed. You may want to add compost or supercompost before planting the seed. Then head to the next patch if there are any left, or a bank or the Grand Exchange when you're finished with all the patches.",
"Falador lodestone - Teleports near the north gate.",
"Falador Teleport - Teleports to the city square near the north gate. Requires level 37 Magic and an air runes, a water rune, and a law rune. Falador teleport tablet may also be used.",
"Teleport to South Falador - Teleports to the south gate southern entrance. Unlocked at the Livid Farm, requires level 72 Magic, being on the Lunar Spellbook and two astral runes, a law rune, and two air runes.",
"Skills necklace - Teleports to the Mining Guild's entrance.",
"Falador",
"Ectophial teleport to the Ectofuntus (requires Ghosts Ahoy).",
"Use Canifis lodestone, run east to the Ectofuntus.",
"Fairy ring ALQ to the Haunted Woods, run east.",
"Port Phasmatys",
"From Taverley, venture west across White Wolf Mountain or take the tunnel below (requires completion of the Fishing Contest quest).",
"Teleport to Catherby directly by using the Catherby lodestone.",
"Teleport to Seers' Village lodestone and walk south-east.",
"Cast Camelot Teleport or use a Camelot teleport tablet and walk south-east.",
"Catherby",
"Falador, Port Phasmatys, Catherby and Manor Farm",
"2 Farming",
"Explorer's ring 3 (recommended)",
"Money making guide/Farming marigolds",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Farming_marigolds?oldid=36948872",
"Farming marigolds",
"farming-morchella-mushrooms.standard",
"Can be done every 200 minutes; a run takes about 2 minutes.",
"200 minutes",
"There are three mushroom patches. Start at the mushroom patch west of Canifis. The simplest way to get to the patch is by using the fairy ring CKS, which teleports you steps from the patch. Once you're there, harvest the mushrooms and plant new ones. Next teleport to the Isafdar patch directly with the Tirannwn quiver 3 or use the Tirannwn lodestone and go west through the dense forest then run south to the Isafdar mushroom patch. Harvest and replant the mushrooms. Finally, if you have 80 Necromancy, teleport to the City of Um using the Underworld Grimoire (Um smithy) and go west to the mushroom patch. Harvest, and replant the mushrooms there. Alternatively, if the Passing bracelet is obtained, players can rub the bracelet and choose the first option (City of Um: Hanging Gardens) The patches have a growing time of 240 minutes - reduced to 200 if the spores are planted with a Sunburst bracelet equipped.",
"The Morytania achievements help immensely for growing morchella mushrooms -- after completing the Medium achievements, the Morytania patch will be immune from disease, so no supercompost is necessary. However, it is advised to use supercompost on the Isafdar patch as this may become diseased. Also, the Pharm Ecology relic power protects the mushroom patches, laying off the need for supercompost.",
"Mushroom patches",
