"killing-muspah.standard",
"Kill muspah. Collect the drops listed in Outputs and restock supplies between trips.",
"Your actual profit may be higher or lower depending on your speed. Profit or loss from creating pouches from spines is not included.",
"Force muspah, bladed muspah, and throwing muspah are unlocked after completing Fate of the Gods. They are found in the Cradle in Freneskae where they were originally encountered during the quest. The fastest means of reaching the world gate to enter Freneskae is by teleporting with a Sixth-Age circuit after having this teleport added by the Guthixian High Druid.",
"Freneskae may be accessed after starting Fate of the Gods, by means of the World Gate, located north of the Arandar and south of the Eagles' Peak. Fate of the Gods takes place almost entirely on Freneskae, and after the quest is completed, Freneskae remains open for exploration. To access Freneskae through the world gate, it must be dialled to .",
"The world gate itself may be reached by.",
"Use Sixth-Age circuit teleport to World Gate (option 2).",
"Use Quest Cape or master quest cape teleport to World Gate (option 0).",
