"killing-unicows.standard",
"Kill unicows. Collect the drops listed in Outputs and restock supplies between trips.",
"With an Ardougne cloak, the unicows have a chance of dropping noted unicorn horns instead, saving inventory space. Due to an update, this noted effect is permanently enabled and there is no way to disable it in order to guaranteed un-noted drops. However noted unicorn horn can be un-noted one at a time by either a right-click option on the Altar, or 'use' the horn on the Altar. With one unicorn horn and a war tortoise and inventory full of cowhides, it is possible to create and kill up to 45 unicows per trip. This will usually generate about 90 unicorn horns. Banking may be done via the fairy ring (code DJP). Returning to the Tower of Life may be done via the fairy ring once more or using the Ardougne cloak teleport to the Kandarin Monastery. Six or more trips per hour are feasible.",
"The Tower of Life is found south of East Ardougne. It can be easily accessed using.",
"Using Ardougne cloak or Kandarin monastery Teleport, you can teleport to the nearby Monastery which is a short walk from the tower.",
"Use Ardougne Teleport brings you to the East Ardougne marketplace, with the tower to the south.",
"Fairy ring DJP brings you right next to the tower. Use of fairy rings requires partial completion of the quest A Fairy Tale II - Cure a Queen.",
"Tower of Life (building)",
"The Ardougne lodestone is located just north of the city, directly southwest of Manor Farm.",
"The Ardougne Teleport spell teleports the player to the centre of Ardougne market, requiring completion of the Plague City quest.",
"The Ardougne cloak 1 can be used to teleport to the Ardougne Monastery, just south of the city.",
"Once per day, the Ardougne cloak 2/3 can be used to teleport to Manor Farm, just north of the city.",
"Ardougne",
