"Making aggression potions",
"making-bomb-vials.standard",
"Use the crafting skill to blow molten glass into bomb vials. A single inventory, in addition to banking (with presets), can be done in just under a minute, which works out to 1830 vials an hour. A more sedate 10 seconds to bank gives 1,680 bomb vials an hour.",
"Money making guide/Making bomb vials",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Making_bomb_vials?oldid=36473773",
"Making bomb vials",
"making-botanist-s-amulets.balls-of-wool",
"The botanist's amulet is in high demand because when the amulet is worn, there is approximately a 5% chance to brew a 4-dose potion instead of a 3-dose potion while training Herblore. As Herblore is one of the most expensive skills to train, the amulet provides a good way of saving gp and increasing total dosages.",
"The first step of this method requires combining silver bars and jades in a furnace. You can go to the Lumbridge furnace and use the convenient bank chest at the nearby Lumbridge Market to make unstrung jade amulets. Alternatively, if you have unlocked access to the furnace at Edgeville, you will be able to run supplies to and from the nearby bank easily. You can store your silver bars in the metal bank.",
"Upon completion of all of the unstrung amulets, proceed to string all of them using balls of wool. The stringing should not take nearly as long as either of the two other processes.",
"The final step in this method is to enchant the amulets by using the Lvl-2 Enchant spell in Standard spells. Wield a Staff of air to save the air rune cost.",
"Edgeville or Combat academy bank",
"Amulet mould (if not already in your tool belt)",
"Artisan's outfit",
"Money making guide/Making botanist's amulets",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Making_botanist's_amulets?oldid=37087833",
"Making botanist's amulets",
