"making-torstol-incense-sticks.standard",
"Torstol incense sticks are used by wealthy players for their global experience boost. While it would technically be faster to use infernal magic incense sticks in the process, there is no profit margin for whoever makes those, and as such they will hardly ever be found on the Grand Exchange. It takes 5 ticks to apply the ashes to the sticks, then 6 ticks to apply the herb to the ashed sticks. Accounting for some extra time for banking, 500 ashed and herbed incense sticks per hour is a reasonable expectation.",
"The Prayer experience from ashing the magic incense sticks is identical to the experience from scattering the infernal ashes, but unlike typical Prayer and Firemaking training methods, incense turns the logs and ashes into a sellable product rather than simply being destroyed, making it a rare method of training either skill that can actually make money in the process. It is slower Prayer XP than scattering the ashes due to the time required per ash and about half the time being taken up with applying the herb instead, to say nothing of using altars for Prayer training, but it is Prayer XP at a profit nonetheless.",
"Money making guide/Making torstol incense sticks",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Making_torstol_incense_sticks?oldid=36473723",
"Making torstol incense sticks",
"making-ultracompost.standard",
"With Infernus pyroclasts tradeable on the Grand Exchange, ultracompost production is no longer limited by the manure dropping rate of dragons at the Anachronia dinosaur farm. There are 7 compost bins, allowing for 105 buckets of ultracompost roughly every 90 minutes, effectively 70 buckets an hour. Compost bin locations: Manor Farm, Catherby, Taverley, South Falador, East of Canifis, Herblore Habitat, and Prifddinas.",
"Compost bins; Manor Farm is one option",
"Plague's End (for maximum production)",
"Money making guide/Making ultracompost",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Making_ultracompost?oldid=36461773",
"Making ultracompost",
"making-ultracompost-infernus-pyroclasts.standard",
"Can be done every 28 hours; a run takes about 20 minutes.",
"28 hours",
"With the release of Garden of Kharid, the process for making compost has been streamlined.",
"Deposit 1,000 noted infernus pyroclasts into any compost bin.",
"Return after about 28 hours to collect the ultracompost and deposit it to a tool leprechaun until the compost bin is empty.",
"A quick way to do this while avoiding the UI is to \"use\" the ultracompost on the leprechaun, typing in any number 28 or above (99 works) into the prompt and hitting enter.",
"Withdraw the ultracompost from the tool leprechaun in noted form (via the \"Noted-X\" option in the storage interface) and sell it.",
"50 required to access the Sydekix's Shop of Balance",
"Buckets All the Way Down unlocked from Sydekix's Shop of Balance",
"Money making guide/Making ultracompost (infernus pyroclasts)",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Making_ultracompost_(infernus_pyroclasts)?oldid=36783073",
"Making ultracompost (infernus pyroclasts)",
"making-unfinished-avantoe-potions.standard",
"Avantoe potion (unfinished) are used to create super energy potions. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean avantoe to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange.",
"Using portable wells gives a 5% chance of making an extra potion and the scroll of cleansing gives a permanent 10% chance of not using up an ingredient when making potions. The bonuses of these two items increase the number of unfinished potions you can make, and the portable well also makes the process less click-intensive. With a portable well placed next to a bank chest, click on the bank chest and deposit your inventory and withdraw 14 herbs and 14 vials of water by using a bank preset, and repeat.",
"There is usually a portable well placed and maintained by someone else next to the bank chest in the Lumbridge Market in world 84. However, if there isn't one and no-one else provides one within a reasonable amount of time, you may have to use your own wells.",
"The bonuses of these two items increase the number of unfinished potions you can make, and the portable well also makes the process less click-intensive. With a portable well placed next to a bank chest, click on the bank chest and deposit your inventory and withdraw 14 herbs and 14 vials of water by using a bank preset, and repeat.",
"49 Herblore",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished avantoe potions",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Making_unfinished_avantoe_potions?oldid=36714081",
"Making unfinished avantoe potions",
"making-unfinished-dwarf-weed-potions.standard",
"Dwarf weed potion (unfinished) are used to create super ranging potions. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean dwarf weed to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange. It is possible to obtain rates of up to 2800 potions per hour by using a beast of burden such as a pack yak along with bank presets to optimize time spent potion making. This will require a higher intensity in order to manage both inventories.",
"Using portable wells gives a 5% chance of making an extra potion, Brooch of the Gods gives an additional 5%, and the Modified botanist's mask gives another 5%. The scroll of cleansing gives a permanent 10% chance of not using up an ingredient when making potions. The bonuses of these items increase the number of unfinished potions you can make, and the portable well also makes the process less click-intensive. With a portable well placed next to a bank chest, click on the bank chest and deposit your inventory and withdraw 14 herbs and 14 vials of water by using a bank preset, and repeat.",
"Using portable wells gives a 5% chance of making an extra potion, Brooch of the Gods gives an additional 5%, and the Modified botanist's mask gives another 5%. The bonuses of these items increase the number of unfinished potions you can make, and the portable well also makes the process less click-intensive. With a portable well placed next to a bank chest, click on the bank chest and deposit your inventory and withdraw 14 herbs and 14 vials of water by using a bank preset, and repeat.",
"There is usually a portable well placed and maintained by someone else next to the bank chest in Fort Forinthry in world 84. However, if there isn't one and no-one else provides one within a reasonable amount of time, you may have to use your own wells.",
"70 Herblore",
"Money making guide/Making unfinished dwarf weed potions",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Making_unfinished_dwarf_weed_potions?oldid=37166926",
"Making unfinished dwarf weed potions",
"making-unfinished-fellstalk-potions.standard",
"Fellstalk potion (unfinished) are used to create Prayer renewals. Because these are often used to train Herblore, and adding clean fellstalk to a vial of water gives little experience, many players avoid the tedium of making unfinished potions and buy them directly from the Grand Exchange.",
