"opening-muddy-chests.free-to-play",
"Assumes the guide's 560 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Located in the centre of the Lava Maze, the muddy chest contains various rewards. Opening it consumes a muddy key. Muddy keys have a buying limit of 100 on the Grand Exchange, but they are relatively easy to buy since they have a high trade volume.",
"Make your way to the Lava Maze with 28 muddy keys in your inventory either by running, using teleports, or using the canoe. Slash the webs apart and avoid the hellhounds (or turn on Protect from Melee), and make your way to the muddy chest at the end. Run to the nearest cape seller/banker to the west of the Lava Maze and refill your inventory with keys using a preset. Sometimes a roaming banker will be within sight when you leave the maze so use this bank when possible.",
"Free players will either get 5000 or 15000 coins from the chest, with an estimated average of 7500 per opening. This means only one inventory space is required for all the loot. Use Surge to optimise your running time.",
"The obelisk in level 44 Wilderness is the closest, from there run a short distance to the southeast.",
"The obelisk in level 35 Wilderness is a bit further, the maze entrance is towards the northwest.",
"The obelisk in level 27 Wilderness is the furthest but still practical, run a little distance to the north.",
"Players can also teleport to the Lava Maze by way of a lava titan's special ability.",
"Located in the centre of the Lava Maze, the muddy chest contains various rewards. Opening it consumes a muddy key.",
"Lava Maze",
"Muddy chest",
"Armour for travelling through the Lava Maze.",
"70 Combat (recommended)",
"5 Agility (recommended)",
"Money making guide/Opening muddy chests",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Opening_muddy_chests?oldid=37175563",
"Opening muddy chests",
"opening-muddy-chests.no-beast-of-burden",
"Assumes the guide's 280 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Starting your run, fill your inventory with muddy keys. Teleport to the level 44 obelisk using an obelisk shard or the portable obelisk. Make your way through the maze, slashing the webs apart and avoiding the hellhounds. Having a kitchen built in Fort Forinthry gives a 100% success rate in slashing spider webs. Reach the muddy chest at the end. Avoid the aggressive ripper demons inside the muddy chest area or turn on Protect from Melee/Deflect Melee. When finished, teleport out of the maze. Bank, heal if necessary, and refill your inventory with keys using a preset. Rinse and repeat.",
"Be wary as your first used key can drop items on the floor. Dive and Mobile can be used to optimise your running time. Out of the three ripper demons at the end of the maze, only the westernmost one is in aggro range of the chest. The best way to deal with it is to lure it north, outside of the fence, then east and directly south, on top of the earth staff spawn. Then teleport out so it doesn't follow you.",
"Use Starting your run, fill your inventory with muddy keys. Teleport to the level 44 obelisk using an obelisk shard or the portable obelisk. Make your way through the maze, slashing the webs apart and avoiding the hellhounds. Having a kitchen built in Fort Forinthry gives a 100% success rate in slashing spider webs. Reach the muddy chest at the end. Avoid the aggressive ripper demons inside the muddy chest area or turn on Protect from Melee/Deflect Melee. When finished, teleport out of the maze. Bank, heal if necessary, and refill your inventory with keys using a preset. Rinse and repeat.",
"Obelisk shard or Portable obelisk",
"Hard Wilderness achievements completed to choose the destination of obelisk teleports",
"War's Retreat Teleport optional or other emergency teleport",
"No Beast of Burden",
"opening-muddy-chests.pack-yak",
"Assumes the guide's 850 actions per hour. Adjust it to your own pace.",
"Starting your run, fill your inventory and pack yak with muddy keys. Teleport to the level 44 obelisk using an obelisk shard or the portable obelisk. Make your way through the maze, slashing the webs apart and avoiding the hellhounds. Having a kitchen built in Fort Forinthry gives a 100% success rate in slashing spider webs. Reach the muddy chest at the end. Avoid the aggressive ripper demons inside the muddy chest area or turn on Protect from Melee/Deflect Melee. When finished, teleport out of the maze. Bank, heal if necessary, and refill your yak and inventory with keys using a preset. Rinse and repeat.",
"Be wary as your first used key can drop items on the floor. Dive and Mobile can be used to optimise your running time. Out of the three ripper demons at the end of the maze, only the westernmost one is in aggro range of the chest. The best way to deal with it is to lure it north, outside of the fence, then east and directly south, on top of the earth staff spawn.",
"Use Starting your run, fill your inventory and pack yak with muddy keys. Teleport to the level 44 obelisk using an obelisk shard or the portable obelisk. Make your way through the maze, slashing the webs apart and avoiding the hellhounds. Having a kitchen built in Fort Forinthry gives a 100% success rate in slashing spider webs. Reach the muddy chest at the end. Avoid the aggressive ripper demons inside the muddy chest area or turn on Protect from Melee/Deflect Melee. When finished, teleport out of the maze. Bank, heal if necessary, and refill your yak and inventory with keys using a preset. Rinse and repeat.",
