"picking-cabbages.standard",
"Put War's Retreat Teleport on your main skilling/non-combat action bar and have that as your primary bar. Right click on your (equipped) explorer's ring 3, cabbage-port, then start plucking in organised fashion so you can always walk two steps over to the next cabbage. Going across rows each time is advised. Once your inventory is full, teleport to War's Retreat and go to the bank chest. Hit 3 to bank-all and Esc to exit with your cursor already on your explorer's ring. Repeat.",
"As an alternative for free players without the War's Retreat Teleport, the Skull of Remembrance from the quest The Death of Chivalry can be used to teleport close to a bank chest.",
"Low-level players should beware Goblin Raids spawning on the cabbage patch, although Goblin Raiders are not aggressive.",
"Falador Cabbage Patch, War's Retreat",
"Explorer's ring 3 or better",
"Money making guide/Picking cabbages",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Picking_cabbages?oldid=36948354",
"Picking cabbages",
"picking-cadava-berries.standard",
"Cadava berries are valuable as ingredients in Necromancy potions. They can be picked from cadava bushes south of Varrock. There are 3 of them with 2 berries each, or 6 in total.",
"Due to the long respawn time, this method requires world switching to gather berries more quickly. The gathering speed would depend on how fast world switching can be done.",
"After 5 worlds, you should have 28 berries. Banking is fastest with War's Retreat Teleport, then use Archaeology journal to teleport back. If you have not unlocked War's Retreat Teleport, you can bank with the journal. 25 runs are possible in 1 hour.",
"Cadava berries are in high demand and the bushes are not instanced, so there might be occasional competition making it take longer to gather berries.",
"South of Varrock",
"Money making guide/Picking cadava berries",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Picking_cadava_berries?oldid=36447549",
"Picking cadava berries",
"picking-coconuts.standard",
"Can be done every 270 minutes; a run takes about 5 minutes.",
"270 minutes",
"240 Coins are needed only for the charter ship; the Karamja lodestone is no cost. Juju teleport spiritbag cost can be eliminated using the witchdoctor mask. Coconuts grow on palm trees, and they're used to make coconut milk, used in high-level Herblore. They're also used to pay farmers to look after magic trees. Once a palm tree has grown fully, it can be harvested repeatedly, with a coconut growing back every 45 minutes for a maximum of six. Harvest the coconuts and note them with the tool leprechaun at any patch if inventory becomes full.",
"Enter the maze by following Elkoy, use the spirit tree to get to the Tree Gnome Stronghold patch, above the agility course.",
"Teleport to Castle wars using a ring of duelling, use Fairy ring code CIQ, or the Yanille lodestone for the fruit tree patch near Tree Gnome Village, west of the maze.",
"Charter a ship to Brimhaven, use a brimhaven tablet, or take the Karamja lodestone to get to the patch, south of the docks.",
"Teleport to Catherby lodestone and run south-east to the tree patch.",
"Seven fruit tree patches",
"68 Farming",
"78 for Giant ent",
"Plague's End for access to Prifddinas",
"The Path of Glouphrie for Spirit trees",
"PRISONER_OF_GLOUPHRIE",
"The Prisoner of Glouphrie for Gnome gliders",
"Palm trees already planted in patches",
"Money making guide/Picking coconuts",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Picking_coconuts?oldid=37011015",
"Picking coconuts",
"picking-curry-leaves.standard",
"Can be done every 270 minutes; a run takes about 4 minutes.",
"Curry leaves grow on curry trees, and they're used in Cooking and Farming. Once a curry tree has grown fully, it can be harvested repeatedly, with a curry leaf growing back every 45 minutes for a maximum of six.",
"Teleport to Castle Wars using a ring of duelling, use Fairy ring code CIQ, or the Yanille lodestone for the fruit tree patch near Tree Gnome Village, west of the maze.",
"Use Charter a ship to Brimhaven, use a brimhaven tablet, or take the Karamja lodestone to get to the patch, south of the docks.",
"Witchdoctor mask or Juju teleport spiritbag",
"Curry trees already planted in patches",
"Money making guide/Picking curry leaves",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Picking_curry_leaves?oldid=37011047",
"Picking curry leaves",
"picking-glowing-fungus.standard",
"Picking up glowing fungus and dropping it turns it into ashes, highly valued for Necromancy as an ingredient of ghostly ink. The Underworld Grimoire is required as it automatically banks any ashes picked up and the glowing fungus is very remote. Once you have picked up a piece of the fungus, drag and drop it onto your action bar. Once it is bound to a key, you can hold that key indefinitely and any fungus you hold and further pick would automatically be dropped. Click the dropped ashes to open the loot interface, then you can use space to loot and bank all ashes on the ground at once. One inventory can be banked in about 36 seconds, or 100 loads in 1 hour (although you don't have to bank 28 ashes exactly every time). Glowing fungus regrows almost instantly.",
"There is no direct path to the mine; the fastest method to reach the entrance is to use a Games necklace or Drakan's medallion to teleport to Burgh de Rott and run west. Otherwise, players must travel through Mort Myre Swamp.",
"Abandoned Mine",
"Underworld Grimoire 1 or better",
"Money making guide/Picking glowing fungus",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Picking_glowing_fungus?oldid=36861802",
"Picking glowing fungus",
"picking-papayas.standard",
"Papaya fruits grow on papaya trees, and they're used in Summoning, Hunter and Farming. Once a papaya tree has grown fully, it can be harvested repeatedly, with a papaya growing back every 45 minutes for a maximum of six.",
"78 Summoning",
"Papaya trees already planted in patches",
"Money making guide/Picking papayas",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Picking_papayas?oldid=37023468",
"Picking papayas",
"picking-potatoes.standard",
"Raw potatoes are the base ingredient for all types of potatoes with toppings. There is a consistent demand for raw potatoes on the Grand Exchange, and someone has to pick them!",
"Potatoes can be found in potato fields, and the best free-to-play location is north of the Lumbridge cow pen. Starting off at the Varrock lodestone, walk the road south, going through the fence. The potato field is directly to the south east. Use of Surge can reduce travel time.",
"Pick the potatoes - travelling diagonally along the rows is most effective. Members can store potatoes in sacks to reduce the amount of time spent banking, and increase profit earned per hour. Potato seeds are sometimes obtained from picking potatoes on members worlds; it is therefore recommended to do this method on a free to play world.",
"Teleport to the Burthorpe lodestone and bank there. Teleport back to the Varrock lodestone and run back to the potato field to continue picking potatoes.",
"Lumbridge potato field",
"Money making guide/Picking potatoes",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Picking_potatoes?oldid=36473288",
"Picking potatoes",
"picking-primal-fruit.standard",
"Can be done every 360 minutes (fruit and cactus regrow every 120 minutes); a run takes about 6 minutes.",
"360 minutes (fruit and cactus regrow every 120 minutes)",
"See also primal fruit pulp for info on fruit. Harvesting primal fruit allows a player to get farming XP while collecting valuable fruit. Once a plant has fully grown, fruit can be collected regularly without additional input. Higher level fruit gives more experience, more pulp and often more profit. The master farmer gives a 10% chance to get an additional piece of fruit at the bush or fruit tree patches. Unlocking Bountiful Harvest 2 from the Garden of Kharid gives a 7% chance of an additional item upon each harvest.",
"A primal fruit run consists of 3 parts.",
"For the bush patches a wolpertinger doubles yield and XP. The bush can be clicked once per tick for faster harvesting. The patches are at.",
"Champion's guild, reachable from the Combat bracelet or Varrock lodestone.",
"Rimmington, reachable from a (modified) Teleport to house or Port Sarim lodestone.",
"Use Champion's guild, reachable from the Combat bracelet or Varrock lodestone.",
"Use Rimmington, reachable from a (modified) Teleport to house or Port Sarim lodestone.",
"4 × cactus patches, 8 × fruit tree patches, 5 × bush patches",
"72 for Anachronia Teleport",
