"Swarm fishing",
"taking-eggs-from-larder.standard",
"Players can collect a lot of eggs from the larder in a player-owned house in a short period of time. Stand between the sink space and the larder so that the servant always returns to the same location. To collect eggs from the larder.",
"Hold down \"3\".",
"Click the larder every 1 tick (or spam click) until inventory has at least 26 eggs.",
"Call the servant for the first time (after the first inventory just click on the servant).",
"Use an egg on the butler and type how many eggs to transfer to your bank.",
"Player-owned house's kitchen",
"60 Invention",
"Have an oak or teak larder built in your player-owned house",
"Money making guide/Taking eggs from larder",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Taking_eggs_from_larder?oldid=36473765",
"Taking eggs from larder",
"taking-vials-of-water-from-a-portable-well.standard",
"Vials of water are often in high demand because they must be used with a herb in order to make an unfinished potion for the Herblore skill. Players often buy them in bulk.",
"A portable well can be placed next to a bank, and has a right click option to take vials of water. You then need to type the number of vials to be taken. The exact number does not need to be typed and as such typing 111 or 33 may be faster than typing 28 exactly, as any excess over the number of available inventory spaces will simply be ignored.",
"A bank preset with an empty inventory may be used to speed up collecting as activating the preset by hotkey will both empty the inventory of vials and close the bank interface. Using this method is is possible to obtain an inventory of vials in under 6 seconds, resulting in 16,800 vials of water per hour. This number may be higher with practice.",
"Bankstanding",
"Money making guide/Taking vials of water from a portable well",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Taking_vials_of_water_from_a_portable_well?oldid=36473822",
"Taking vials of water from a portable well",
"tanning-hides.black-dragonhide",
"Black dragon leather is used to train Crafting, and it is always in high demand. Because black dragonhide must be tanned into leather before it can be crafted, tanning the hides in bulk can be highly profitable. It should be noted that black dragonhide has a buy limit of 10,000 hides every 4 hours. It is also possible to work around the limit by directly trading with other players or by using alternate accounts.",
"Because the price difference between hides and leather can be fairly small, it is important to buy the hides for a low price and sell the leather for a high price; you can lose out on up to 50% of the profit if you are not patient. Test the profit by buying one black dragonhide and one black dragon leather. If the difference between the two is less than 200, it may be better to tan other dragonhides instead.",
"It should take you around 10 minutes to tan 10,000 hides.",
"To tan dragon leather with maximum efficiency, deploy a portable crafter near a bank or bank chest (for example, near the bank chest in Castle Wars), make a preset with 28 black dragonhide, and load it. Then right-click the crafter and choose Tan Leather. Alternatively, you can right-click configure the portable crafter so that the default left-click action is tan hides.",
"To tan dragon leather with maximum efficiency, deploy a portable crafter near a bank or bank chest (for example, near the bank chest in Castle Wars), make a preset with 28 black dragonhide, and load it. Then right-click the crafter and choose Tan Leather. Alternatively, you can right-click configure the portable crafter so that the default left-click action is tan hides. You can also use portable crafters on the one already deployed to increase its duration by five minutes per crafter. It is also possible to avoid the cost of the portable crafters by using those placed by other players. The Lumbridge Market in World 84 almost always has a portable crafter set up next to the bank chest.",
"Zoom in and adjust your camera so the portable crafter and the bank would be next to each other.",
"Fort Forinthry (W84 Portable Skilling)",
"Money making guide/Tanning hides",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Tanning_hides?oldid=36862088",
"Tanning hides",
"tanning-hides.blue-dragonhide",
"Blue dragon leather is used to train Crafting, and it is always in high demand. Because blue dragonhide must be tanned into leather before it can be crafted, tanning the hides in bulk can be highly profitable. It should be noted that blue dragonhide has a buy limit of 10,000 hides every 4 hours. It is also possible to work around the limit by directly trading with other players or by using alternate accounts.",
"Because the price difference between hides and leather can be fairly small, it is important to buy the hides for a low price and sell the leather for a high price; you can lose out on up to 50% of the profit if you are not patient. Test the profit by buying one blue dragonhide and one blue dragon leather. If the difference between the two is less than 200, it may be better to tan other dragonhides instead.",
"To tan dragon leather with maximum efficiency, deploy a portable crafter near a bank or bank chest (for example, near one of the bank chests in Fort Forinthry), make a preset with 28 blue dragonhide, and load it. Then right-click the crafter and choose Tan Leather. Alternatively, you can right-click configure the portable crafter so that the default left-click action is tan hides.",
"To tan dragon leather with maximum efficiency, deploy a portable crafter near a bank or bank chest (for example, near one of the bank chests in Fort Forinthry), make a preset with 28 blue dragonhide, and load it. Then right-click the crafter and choose Tan Leather. Alternatively, you can right-click configure the portable crafter so that the default left-click action is tan hides. You can also use portable crafters on the one already deployed to increase its duration by five minutes per crafter. It is also possible to avoid the cost of the portable crafters by using those placed by other players. Fort Forinthry in World 84 almost always has a portable crafter set up next to the bank chest.",
"Fort Forinthry recommended",
"2 Crafting",
"tanning-hides.green-dragonhide",
"Green dragon leather is used to train Crafting, and it is always in high demand. Because green dragonhide must be tanned into leather before it can be crafted, tanning the hides in bulk can be highly profitable. It should be noted that green dragonhide has a buy limit of 10,000 hides every 4 hours. It is also possible to work around the limit by directly trading with other players or by using alternate accounts.",
"Because the price difference between hides and leather can be fairly small, it is important to buy the hides for a low price and sell the leather for a high price; you can lose out on up to 50% of the profit if you are not patient. Test the profit by buying one green dragonhide and one green dragon leather. If the difference between the two is less than 200, it may be better to tan other dragonhides instead.",
"To tan dragon leather with maximum efficiency, deploy a portable crafter near a bank or bank chest (for example, near one of the bank chests in Fort Forinthry), make a preset with 28 green dragonhide, and load it. Then right-click the crafter and choose Tan Leather. Alternatively, you can right-click configure the portable crafter so that the default left-click action is tan hides.",
"To tan dragon leather with maximum efficiency, deploy a portable crafter near a bank or bank chest (for example, near one of the bank chests in Fort Forinthry), make a preset with 28 green dragonhide, and load it. Then right-click the crafter and choose Tan Leather. Alternatively, you can right-click configure the portable crafter so that the default left-click action is tan hides. You can also use portable crafters on the one already deployed to increase its duration by five minutes per crafter. It is also possible to avoid the cost of the portable crafters by using those placed by other players. Fort Forinthry in World 84 almost always has a portable crafter set up next to the bank chest.",
"tanning-hides.royal-dragonhide",
"Royal dragon leather is used to train Crafting, and it is always in high demand. Because Royal dragonhide must be tanned into leather before it can be crafted, tanning the hides in bulk can be highly profitable.",
"Because the price difference between hides and leather can be fairly small, it is important to buy the hides for a low price and sell the leather for a high price; up to 50% of the profit can be lost otherwise. Test the profit by buying one Royal dragonhide and one Royal dragon leather. If the difference between the two is less than 200, it may be worth it to switch to other dragonhides.",
"It should be noted that royal dragonhide has a buylimit of 10,000 every 4 hours. It should take around 10 minutes to tan them. It is possible to work around the limit by letting the order fill while doing other activities, directly trading with other players, or by using alternate accounts.",
"To tan dragon leather with maximum efficiency, deploy a portable crafter near a bank or bank chest (for example, near one of the bank chests in Fort Forinthry), make a preset with 28 royal dragonhide, and load it. Then right-click the crafter and choose Tan Leather. Additionally, portable crafters can be used on the one already deployed to increase its duration by five minutes per crafter.",
"To tan dragon leather with maximum efficiency, deploy a portable crafter near a bank or bank chest (for example, near one of the bank chests in Fort Forinthry), make a preset with 28 royal dragonhide, and load it. Then right-click the crafter and choose Tan Leather. Additionally, portable crafters can be used on the one already deployed to increase its duration by five minutes per crafter. It is also possible to avoid the cost of the portable crafters by using those placed by other players. Fort Forinthry on world 84 and the Minigames and D&Ds forum are good places to check.",
"tanning-royal-dragonhide-with-make-leather.standard",
"While regular tanning can be quite profitable on its own, using the lunar spell Make Leather (which tans five hides at once) can increase the profit by more than 50% while also giving decent Magic experience. The downside is that Make Leather must be unlocked from Livid Farm, which requires 75,000 produce points.",
"Because the price difference between hides and leather can be fairly small, it is important to buy the hides for a low price and sell the leather for a high price; you can lose out on much of the profit or even turn a loss if you are not patient. Test the profit by buying one Royal dragonhide and one Royal dragon leather. If the difference between the two is less than 200, it may be worth it to switch to a different hide type. In some cases the profit can be more than 500 coins -- the guide prices on the Grand Exchange are not always indicative of the current trading price.",
"83 Magic",
"Make Leather spell unlocked from Livid Farm (75,000 produce points)",
"Lunar spellbook active (Lunar Diplomacy)",
"Money making guide/Tanning royal dragonhide with Make Leather",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Tanning_royal_dragonhide_with_Make_Leather?oldid=37193568",
"Tanning royal dragonhide with Make Leather",
"transmuting-onyx-dust.standard",
"Can be done every 4 hours; a run takes about 0.35 minutes.",
"Onyx dust is commonly dropped from Raksha, Arch-Glacor, Croesus, TzKal-Zuk, elite dungeons, and Rasial. 100 dust is needed to make an uncut onyx. There is a 1,000 buy limit per four hours. To work around this, players can let the order fill while doing other activities, trade directly with other players, or use alternate accounts.",
"The diviner's outfit will also increase experience gained by up to 6%.",
"Transmuting onyx dust.",
"97 Divination",
"Money making guide/Transmuting onyx dust",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Transmuting_onyx_dust?oldid=37145280",
"Transmuting onyx dust",
"using-the-auto-disassembler-mk-ii-to-make-empty-divine-charge.standard",
"Can be done every 216 hours; a run takes about 32 minutes.",
"216 hours",
"II. The profit gained from this activity will be lower than shown on this page if you are using the regular auto disassembler.",
"You will first need to have built a auto disassembler, then create the auto disassembler mk. II. You can build an auto disassembler mk. II in the Invention Guild with 81 Invention. However, this guide assumes that you have 105 Invention to have researched empty divine charge blueprint and junk chance reduction 9.",
"26,000 maple logs will be disassembled in 9 days, taking 34 divine charges and producing 15,340 simple parts which will make 767 divine charge (empty). It takes 30 minutes to create the divine charges, and 2 minutes to add the logs and collect the parts.",
"With a jumbo generator, up to three machines can be run at a time, potentially resulting in multiplying the profit, at the expense of being limited in terms of what other machines can be used. Additionally, with a fully upgraded Workshop in Fort Forinthry, five can be used, but there will be no power left for any other machines.",
"To allow profit to be easily calculated for any combination of machines, this page calculates profit on a per-machine basis.",
"101 for empty divine charges",
"105 for junk chance reduction 9",
"auto disassembler",
"auto disassembler mk. II",
"Built an auto disassembler then an auto disassembler mk. II",
"Money making guide/Using the auto disassembler mk. II to make empty divine charge",
"https://runescape.wiki/w/Money_making_guide/Using_the_auto_disassembler_mk._II_to_make_empty_divine_charge?oldid=36787861",
"Using the auto disassembler mk. II to make empty divine charge",
